    <main>
        <h1>LeetCode 2409: Count Days Spent Together (C++)</h1>
        <div class="problem-description">
            <p><strong>Problem:</strong>
                Alice and Bob are traveling to Rome for separate business meetings. You are given 4 strings
                arriveAlice, leaveAlice, arriveBob, and leaveBob. Alice will be in the city from the date
                arriveAlice to leaveAlice (inclusive), while Bob will be in the city from the date arriveBob
                to leaveBob (inclusive). Each date is a string in the format "MM-DD", corresponding to the
                month and day of the date. Return the total number of days that Alice and Bob are in Rome
                together. You can assume that all dates occur in the same calendar year, which is not a leap
                year. Note that the number of days per month can be represented as: [31, 28, 31, 30, 31, 30,
                31, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31].
            </p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong>
                Input: arriveAlice = "08-15", leaveAlice = "08-18", arriveBob = "08-16", leaveBob =
                "08-19"<br>
                Output: 3<br>
                Explanation: Alice will be in Rome from August 15 to August 18. Bob will be in Rome from
                August 16 to August 19. They are both in Rome together on August 16th, 17th, and 18th, so
                the answer is 3.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-container">
            <button class="copy-button" onclick="copyCode(this)">Copy Code</button>
            <pre><code class="language-cpp">class Solution {
public:
    int countDaysTogether(string arriveAlice, string leaveAlice, string arriveBob, string leaveBob) {
        int monthDays[] = {31, 28, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31};

        auto getDay = [&amp;](const string&amp; date) {
            int month = (date[0] - '0') * 10 + (date[1] - '0');
            int day = (date[3] - '0') * 10 + (date[4] - '0');
            int total = day;

            for (int i = 0; i &lt; month - 1; i++) {
                total += monthDays[i];
            }

            return total;
        };

        int aliceStart = getDay(arriveAlice);
        int aliceEnd = getDay(leaveAlice);
        int bobStart = getDay(arriveBob);
        int bobEnd = getDay(leaveBob);

        int overlapStart = max(aliceStart, bobStart);
        int overlapEnd = min(aliceEnd, bobEnd);

        return overlapStart &lt;= overlapEnd ? overlapEnd - overlapStart + 1 : 0;
    }
};</code></pre>
